- M3 insight gate: parses an insight file and checks whys 3–6 levels. This requires judgment to parse "a source that can be changed" — can a script check that? Hard. Half-known: the structural parts (every failure answered, level count, evidence file exists) can be checked; the semantic part (why stops at a changeable source vs "the agent forgot") is a judgment. My #12 says change conditions, not people — a script can check for banned stop-words perhaps. My reading: only structural parts are code-doable; that's the split, and it's honest to say "half".
