- But the bigger question: does installing hooks actually make the agent unable to skip? Facts: PostToolUse only annotates; Stop can force continue with a cap; the agent can edit/disable hooks? Out of scope to edit config, and install is EJ's. So "cannot be skipped" holds only where the hook is installed and the harness honors blocking. For opencode, throw-blocks *reported*. For agy, excluded. So across all harnesses, only some have verified blocking. Half-known overall — but for Claude Code specifically, verified.
